     |   12 +-\n test/yang/python/antlr/float_address_test.cljc     |   28 +-\n test/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc    |   12 +-\n test/yang/python/antlr/linked_safepoint_test.cljc  |    7 +-\n test/yang/python/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc    |    9 +-\n test/yang/safepoint_test.cljc                      |   10 +\n test/yang/typescript/antlr/float_address_test.cljc |    8 +-\n test/yang/typescript/antlr/global_write_test.cljc  |  255 +++\n .../yang/typescript/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc |    3 +-\n .../yang/typescript/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc |   18 +-\n test/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_test.clj          |   16 +-\n test/yang/typescript_callsite_test.cljc            | 1036 ++++++++++\n test/yin/repl/dht_head_test.cljc                   |   37 +-\n test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj                 |    2 +-\n test/yin/repl/dht_test.cljc                        |  206 +-\n test/yin/vm/linker/admission_test.cljc             |  136 +-\n test/yin/vm/linker/dht_end_to_end_test.cljc        |   31 +-\n test/yin/vm/module_test.cljc                       |   19 +\n 509 files changed, 39720 insertions(+), 2234 deletions(-)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-qrglQADY' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-14 23:30:58.834 xcodebuild[10763:131547158]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-14 23:30:59.202 xcodebuild[10763:131547156] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-rjhwXJ2q' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-14 23:31:00.182 xcodebuild[10768:131547182]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-14 23:31:00.480 xcodebuild[10768:131547181] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ndiff --git a/BRIEF-j6g-rebase-fix-findings.md b/BRIEF-j6g-rebase-fix-findings.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..004ecd3b\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/BRIEF-j6g-rebase-fix-findings.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@\n+# J6g rebase fix findings\n+\n+Inspected checkout and origin/master: `746b2c34`. Read the requested\n+`git diff 05a596c5 origin/master -- src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc`.\n+No workload was launched, locally or remotely. Session ID is not exposed by\n+this session's tools; no ID invented.\n+\n+## Attribution\n+\n+The demonstrated failure is a watchdog/worker wire-format mismatch, not an\n+established composition deadlock. `src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj:212` emits\n+`W-SAMPLE` followed by an EDN **map**, containing timestamps and both latency\n+measurements. The original `src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj:28` required\n+`(number? sample)` and set `:sample-error` for every such map. Its kill branch\n+(now at `src/dev/jolt_workload_w_run.clj:155`) reports `:invalid-sample`.\n+The actual deadline is still 300000 ms (`:hard-cap`, now line 167); a failure\n+at ~46 s with `:invalid-sample` is not that cap firing.\n+\n+The original W-STATE was emitted AFTER both `driver/repl-step`/outbox draining\n+and `wake/sleep-fds!` returned (original worker lines 246–253). Thus a\n+W-STATE containing owner-rounds 1 proves round 1 got past those calls.\n+Furthermore, the invalid-sample branch is reached only after a W-SAMPLE line\n+arrives. A well-formed worker sample means B received a reply, which occurs\n+after upgrades, frame construction and A's first positive write. The\n+watchdog's samples remain zero because it rejects the map. Its phase stays\n+\"loading\" because the original worker emitted no W-PHASE lines. These\n+observations cannot establish a first-round block. Exact time spent before\n+the first sample needs the next instrumented run; no measured attribution\n+to frame construction, compilation, or a particular composition call is\n+claimed here.\n+\n+Composition candidates ruled out as explanations of this rejection:\n+\n+- `src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:282` retains the one-argument boot by delegating\n+  to `(boot opts nil)`. Lines 287–289 open a contributed store only when a\n+  composition provides its hooks. Lines 303–310 still return driver state\n+  with engine at `:repl`, adding transport state at sibling `:session` only\n+  when present. This harness selected no durable/DHT store before the fix.\n+- `src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc:823` owns the full owner tick; lines 850–875\n+  step the composition, recheck, step the driver and drain its outbox.\n+  Using only the frozen driver bypassed these host responsibilities, but\n+  that is not evidence of a synchronous first-round block.\n+- `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:1007` selects generic publication policy, falling\n+  back to the store's `:publish-opts` at line 1009. The memory store comes\n+  from `src/cljc/yin/repl/store.cljc:153`. No DHT publication policy is\n+  injected in this harness. A's payload is carried by a separate wsj\n+  instance, never appended to the engine's code-index stream. Code-index\n+  byte budgets therefore do not gate A's paced TCP writes.\n+- `src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc:2895` still exposes the index-publication summary\n+  from `[:indexer :materialization]`; the worker's two cursor paths at\n+  `src/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj:189` remain correct. No path migration was\n+  necessary.\n+\n+Crucially, BOTH harness files also have zero committed diff between 05a596c5\n+and origin/master. The map-versus-number defect exists in that base too.\n+The supplied historical passing run therefore needs its actual launcher,\n+worker and verifier artifacts reconciled by the orchestrator: this exact\n+watchdog cannot accept this exact worker's first sample on either base.\n+This finding does not invalidate separately verified measurements, but\n+prevents attributing their difference to composition drift from these\n+sources alone.\n+\n+## Harness edits\n+\n+Only the two authorized source files were edited, plus this requested brief.\n+\n+- Worker boot explicitly selects `:mem` and supplies nil composition, keeping\n+  the existing memory workload topology. Owner rounds use public\n+  `repl.main/step-all` with no served endpoint and retain its returned state\n+  and output lines. That function performs the single driver step and\n+  outbox drain; the harness does not drain twice.\n+- Added first-two-round W-CALL enter/leave records around step/drain and\n+  socket pumping, and W-PHASE markers for boot, B upgrade, A upgrade, A frame\n+  encoding and running. These expose an actual blocking boundary without\n+  continuous call tracing during the latency cohort.\n+- Ten-second W-PROGRESS includes the original statistics and both original\n+  cursor paths. Watchdog telemetry now retains that progress (and accepts\n+  legacy W-STATE) rather than presenting a permanently empty progress view.\n+- Watchdog accepts the worker's sample maps, validates finite nonnegative\n+  timing fields and timestamp/latency consistency, and samples only the\n+  prospective cohort. It reports both p99 values with the worker's\n+  nearest-rank quantile. It recognizes FAILURE output and requires a passing\n+  W-RESULT alongside a zero process exit.\n+\n+A's 120 s pacing, independent B scheduler at 100 ms, 600-offer cohort,\n+500-sample floor, both 250 ms latency gates, binomial confidence calculation,\n+all 12 worker gates, native socket handling and independent 300 s watchdog\n+are unchanged. No external five-point verifier was edited.\n+\n+## Validation and expected next verification\n+\n+Passed local cljstyle check on both files and `git diff --check`. A temporary\n+Babashka check loaded only watchdog definitions (never its process-launching\n+entry point) and passed valid/map sample acceptance, malformed and NaN sample\n+rejection, timestamp/latency mismatch rejection, cohort filtering,\n+nearest-rank p99, balanced/mismatched call tracing, result/failure/progress\n+parsing, and partial-line assembly. No workload performance claim follows\n+from these checks.\n+\n+Next orchestrator run should survive its first valid B sample, accumulate\n+cohort samples and show both p99s and cursor paths. Setup delays should now\n+have named phases; an actual early owner call stall will retain an active\n+W-CALL until completion or the unchanged 300 s cap. If execution completes,\n+the existing worker gates decide pass/failure; this patch does not promise\n+600 samples or any particular latency. If a composition call actually\n+blocks, send its active trace and run artifacts to the convergence/exception\n+owners. No composition-side change is justified by the current read evidence,\n+and none was made.\n+\n+Historical figures are supplied pre-drift evidence only: 600 samples,\n+3.85 ms RTT p99 / 5.79 ms scheduled-arrival p99 for the named j6ggate29 run;\n+the separately cited 8.75 ms p99 is also historical, not a new measurement.\n+Current-master performance remains unmeasured in this fix round.\ndiff --git a/collab/dao-stream/1794147282000-engineer-step1-invariant-pins.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md b/collab/dao-stream/1794147282000-engineer-step1-invariant-pins.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..efee9c92\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/collab/dao-stream/1794147282000-engineer-step1-invariant-pins.muse-wonder-1.0.findings.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@\n+# Step 1 Findings: Invariant Pins & Non-DHT Fixture Parameterization\n+\n+Created-GMT: 2026-11-08 14:38:30 GMT\n+Created-Local: 2026-11-08 21:38:30 +07\n+Coding-Agent: muse\n+Model: muse-wonder-1.0\n+Session-ID: e8c6e6a5-b58b-45ac-914b-a696f4512f9e\n+\n+## Summary of Deliverable\n+Step 1 of the refactor sequence (docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md §9) is complete. Existing invariants are green and publication-result expectations are explicit. All changes are strictly isolated to `test/yin/repl/` without touching `src/`.\n+\n+## Changes Made\n+- `test/yin/repl/fixture.cljc` (new, 212 lines): Common test constructor providing explicitly injected non-DHT storage backends (`:memory` via `dao.jing.mem`, `:file` via `dao.space.store/open`), publication interpreter wrappers (`observed-backend`, `failable-backend`), and `frontier` extraction.\n+- `test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc`: Decisive publication/frontier/recovery tests parameterized over both backends, plus 6 new pins: frontier-gate agreement after every round, correlated settle-once publication requests, failed-HEAD never advancing the frontier, count-cap mismatch forcing full reconstruction, exact suffix length, and no double settlement.\n+- `test/yin/repl/require_test.cljc`: `shell` and `require-and-apply` parameterized over injected backend; causality/policy tests use explicit memory injection via `prompt-state`.\n+- `test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc`: All shells built through fixture; settlement tests and basic answer tests run across VMs and backends.\n+- `test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc`: Cross-backend proof verifying agreeing frontiers and identical history with `:dht` and `:index-store-spec` both nil.\n+\n+## Verified Test Assertions (JVM Focused)\n+- `yin.repl.index-test`: 27 tests, 569 assertions, 0 failures (baseline: 21 tests, 242 assertions).\n+- `yin.repl.require-test`: 20 tests, 209 assertions, 0 failures (baseline: 20 tests, 172 assertions).\n+- `yin.repl.query-test`: 18 tests, 279 assertions, 0 failures (baseline: 18 tests, 246 assertions).\n+- `yin.repl.store-test`: 28 tests, 145 assertions, 0 failures (baseline: 27 tests, 132 assertions).\ndiff --git a/collab/dao-stream/1794147282000-engineer-step1-invariant-pins.muse-wonder-1.0.stdout.log b/collab/dao-stream/1794147282000-engineer-step1-invariant-pins.muse-wonder-1.0.stdout.log\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..a4884639\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/collab/dao-stream/1794147282000-engineer-step1-invariant-pins.muse-wonder-1.0.stdout.log\n@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@\n+muse: workspace root: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht (cwd default)\n+muse: workspace trust: trusted source=run-flag\n+muse: warning: rules file at /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/CLAUDE.md is ignored this session because AGENTS.md takes precedence in that directory; merge still-applicable guidance into AGENTS.md or remove one of the two files\n+muse: Skills: 38 loaded · 1 warning\n+muse:   `skills_catalog` was trimmed to fit its size limit (32 KB): 1 descriptions compacted, 0 skill ids omitted\n+muse:   Run `muse skills list --source all` for full diagnostics.\n+Completed-GMT: 2026-11-08 14:37:44 GMT\n+Completed-Local: 2026-11-08 21:37:44 +07\n+\n+Step 1 is complete. Existing invariants are green and the publication-result expectations are now explicit, with all changes contained in `test/yin/repl/` and no `src/` edits (uncommitted, for review).\n+\n+**Modified files**\n+\n+- [fixture.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/fixture.cljc) (new) — Gate B's common test constructor: explicitly injected non-DHT backends (`:memory` via `dao.jing.mem/create-content-mem`, `:file` via `dao.space.store/open`), the composition-side publication interpreter (`observed-backend`/`failable-backend` wrapping `:head-fn`), and `frontier` extraction (manifest identity, count, count-cap, cursor). It requires no DHT namespace and constructs no node, socket, follower, or scheduler.\n+- [index_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc) — decisive publication/frontier/recovery tests (§8; spec lines 146, 269, 316, 344, 362, 385, 421, 470, 501, 522, 576) parameterized over both backends, plus six new pins: frontier-gate agreement after every round, correlated settle-once publication requests, failed-HEAD never advancing the frontier, count-cap mismatch forcing full reconstruction, exact suffix length, and no double settlement.\n+- [require_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/require_test.cljc) — `shell`/`require-and-apply` now take the injected backend; prompt-path and rollback tests run on both backends; remaining causality/policy tests use explicit memory injection via `prompt-state`; the DHT composition test (was line 805) is isolated as composition-side for its Step 2 move, still green.\n+- [query_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc) — all shells built through the fixture; settlement tests (283, slow 314, 663) and the basic answer test run on every VM × backend.\n+- [store_test.cljc](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yin-repl-dht/test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc) — new cross-backend proof: same programs publish agreeing frontiers and identical history (modulo session token) on either backend, with `(:dht state)` and `(:index-store-spec state)` both nil.\n+\n+**Diff summary:** 4 files changed, 1022 insertions, 505 deletions, plus the new fixture (212 lines). `git status` shows only these test files; no commits made.\n+\n+**Focused test outcomes** (JVM, run individually, `-e :slow` except the one slow var)\n+\n+| Suite | Baseline | Final |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| `yin.repl.index-test` | 21 tests, 242 assertions | 27 tests, 569 assertions, 0 failures |\n+| `yin.repl.require-test` | 20 tests, 172 assertions | 20 tests, 209 assertions, 0 failures |\n+| `yin.repl.query-test` | 18 tests, 246 assertions | 18 tests, 279 assertions, 0 failures |\n+| `yin.repl.store-test` | 27 tests, 132 assertions | 28 tests, 145 assertions, 0 failures |\n+\n+The slow query settlement var also passes on both backends (16 assertions). Node/Dart lanes were not run (focused JVM runs only, per instructions); the fixture is reader-conditional portable, but that remains unverified. Generated ANTLR parser classes were seeded into the gitignored `build/` cache so the JVM lane could run at all; the working tree carries no build changes.\n+\n+**Finding for Step 2 (not pinned, not fixed — `src/` is out of Step 1 scope):** continuing the shell past a refused publication throws inside `yin.repl.index/notice`, which renders `(name stage)` of the cleared failure and rolls the round back. I verified this on unmodified engine code with a debug script; the failed-HEAD pin therefore proves the retry at the indexer level and documents the defect at the shell level.\ndiff --git a/collab/dao-stream/1794147282000-engineer-step1-invariant-pins.prompt.md b/collab/dao-stream/1794147282000-engineer-step1-invariant-pins.prompt.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..c3526dbc\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/collab/dao-stream/1794147282000-engineer-step1-invariant-pins.prompt.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\n+Created-GMT: 2026-11-08 14:14:42 GMT\n+Created-Local: 2026-11-08 21:14:42 +07\n+Coding-Agent: muse\n+Session-ID: e8c6e6a5-b58b-45ac-914b-a696f4512f9e\n+\n+# Task: Pin baseline contracts and parameterize non-DHT fixtures (Step 1)\n+\n+Role: DaoSpace and DaoJing Storage Engineer\n+\n+Implementers:\n+- Model: muse-wonder-1.0 | Assigned: 2026-11-08 21:14:42 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: Step 1 of spec §9 commit sequence; dedicated scratch worktree datomworld-yin-repl-dht\n+\n+## Governing Specification & Instructions\n+Read first:\n+- `docs/design/yin.repl.dht-composition.md` (specifically §8 Invariants to pin before relocation, and §9 Commit sequence Step 1).\n+- Existing fixtures referenced in spec §8:\n+  - `test/yin/repl/index_test.cljc` (specifically lines around 385, 421, 470, 501, 553, 734)\n+  - `test/yin/repl/require_test.cljc` (specifically lines around 244–766)\n+  - `test/yin/repl/query_test.cljc` (specifically lines around 283, 314, 663)\n+  - `test/yin/repl/store_test.cljc` (specifically lines around 833–1425)\n+\n+## Scope & Acceptance Criteria (Step 1 Exit Condition)\n+Exit condition: Existing