name); a write is `cell/set!`, `js/const-assign!` for a `const`, and\n+     `js/global-set` for a free name — the global object's strict\n+     SetMutableBinding, which reads no value and so invokes no getter.\n    - Numbers are float64 content at the producer: the literal `1` is\n      `(cbor/float64 1.0)`. Strings are `{:js/str s}` when well-formed UTF-16\n      and `{:js/units [u ...]}` otherwise, normalized here the way\n@@ -560,12 +562,18 @@\n         v (u/v value-sym)]\n     (cond\n       (not= :cell (:kind r))\n-      ;; strict code: an undeclared name is a ReferenceError; a declared\n-      ;; global is a known gap (T2 owns the global object's writes)\n-      (u/then (app* 'js/global-get (u/lit (jstr nm)))\n-              (app* 'js/throw-type-error\n-                    (u/lit (jstr (str \"Cannot assign to read only property '\"\n-                                      nm \"' of object\")))))\n+      ;; No lexical binding reaches this name, so the write lands on the\n+      ;; global object's own environment record: a strict SetMutableBinding\n+      ;; (ES2022 §9.1.1.3.3, design §3.1.4 ruling 4, §3.7). Strict mode\n+      ;; refuses to CREATE an implicit global, it does not refuse to update a\n+      ;; global that is already there — `globalThis.saved = null; saved = 7;`\n+      ;; writes even at module goal. A non-writable existing global\n+      ;; (`undefined`) is a TypeError and a name nothing binds at all a\n+      ;; ReferenceError naming it. No `js/global-get` read: assignment\n+      ;; resolves the reference without getting its value, so a global\n+      ;; accessor's getter must stay silent while its setter runs. Declaring\n+      ;; such a global (a script-goal `var`) is design §3.7's deferred slice.\n+      (app* 'js/global-set (u/lit (jstr nm)) v)\n       (:const? r) (u/then (app* 'js/lexical-get (u/v (symbol nm)) (u/lit (jstr nm)))\n                           (app* 'js/const-assign!))\n       (:tdz? r) (u/then (app* 'js/lexical-get (u/v (symbol nm)) (u/lit (jstr nm)))\n@@ -2259,20 +2267,59 @@\n                 (seq-of (lower-stmts ctx stmts)))))\n \n \n+;; =============================================================================\n+;; Call-site occurrence contract C1 (Addendum A, design §2)\n+;; =============================================================================\n+;;\n+;; Every final `:application` occurrence of a tree this namespace answers\n+;; carries the reserved frontend-metadata key `:yang/call-site` with\n+;; version value `1` as a plain node key. Projection\n+;; (`yin.vm/ast-side-tables`) drops the key from canonical rows and emits\n+;; it into the EXISTING generic frontend-metadata side table as\n+;; `[origin root-address path :yang/call-site 1]`, so provenance stays out\n+;; of hashed content: canonical rows, roots, image addresses and\n+;; executable outcomes are unchanged. The walk itself is\n+;; `yang.core.uast/annotate-call-sites`; nothing here re-mints the key or\n+;; the coordinate tuple. It is a distinct key from `:yang/site`, the\n+;; safepoint mark, which travels as node metadata, and a distinct key\n+;; FAMILY again from the exception track's runtime provenance doors\n+;; `cell/dsg__new-provenance` / `cell/dsg__provenance`.\n+;;\n+;; Coverage is all-or-nothing: `yin.vm.encoder/program-batch` and\n+;; `yin.vm.linker.publish/publish-module!` each refuse a tree whose\n+;; markers do not exactly cover its eligible application occurrences. So\n+;; each PUBLIC entry point below finalizes once, over its own complete\n+;; tree, after canonical renaming and tail marking have settled it — and\n+;; the private `lower-unit*` seam exists so `lower-units` and\n+;; `lower-packet` compose unmarked units and walk the composed result a\n+;; single time, rather than leaving their own wrapper applications\n+;; (`js/run-main`, the two `require`s, `js/init!`, the sequencing lambdas)\n+;; unclaimed beside a marked unit.\n+\n (defn lower-module-body\n   \"The module's statements as one node, before the runtime wrapper: what\n-   lowering goldens compare.\"\n+   lowering goldens compare. C1 finalized, like every tree this namespace\n+   answers.\"\n+  [packet]\n+  (u/annotate-call-sites (module-body (context packet))))\n+\n+\n+(defn- lower-unit*\n+  \"`lower-unit` before C1 finalization: the seam `lower-units` and\n+   `lower-packet` compose, so each of them finalizes once over its own\n+   complete tree.\"\n   [packet]\n-  (module-body (context packet)))\n+  (let [ctx (context packet)]\n+    (u/lam [(:this ctx)] (module-body ctx))))\n \n \n (defn lower-unit\n   \"One separately scoped module body as a function of its shared global\n    receiver. Keeping this seam lets a host compose independently parsed\n-   units without concatenating source or reinitializing the runtime.\"\n+   units without concatenating source or reinitializing the runtime.\n+   C1 finalized.\"\n   [packet]\n-  (let [ctx (context packet)]\n-    (u/lam [(:this ctx)] (module-body ctx))))\n+  (u/annotate-call-sites (lower-unit* packet)))\n \n \n (defn- with-runtime\n@@ -2290,10 +2337,11 @@\n (defn lower-units\n   \"A complete program for multiple separately parsed units. The runtime is\n    installed and initialized once; each unit receives its own lexical body\n-   while sharing the same global object and output stream.\"\n+   while sharing the same global object and output stream. C1 finalized\n+   once, over the composed tree.\"\n   ([packets] (lower-units packets {}))\n   ([packets {:keys [prelude], :or {prelude :bundled}}]\n-   (let [units (mapv lower-unit packets)\n+   (let [units (mapv lower-unit* packets)\n          main (names/canonicalize\n                 (app* 'js/run-main\n                       (u/lam ['this]\n@@ -2301,13 +2349,13 @@\n                                (u/seq-nodes\n                                  (mapv (fn [unit] (u/app unit (u/v 'this))) units))\n                                (u/lit :js/undefined)))))]\n-     (with-runtime prelude main))))\n+     (u/annotate-call-sites (with-runtime prelude main)))))\n \n \n (defn lower-packet\n   \"The complete program for one ok packet: the module body run by\n-   `js/run-main`, generated names canonicalized, tail calls marked. Its\n-   value is `{:js/out [...] :js/uncaught nil-or-snapshot}`.\n+   `js/run-main`, generated names canonicalized, tail calls marked, C1\n+   finalized. Its value is `{:js/out [...] :js/uncaught nil-or-snapshot}`.\n \n    `:prelude` selects how the runtime profile arrives: `:bundled` (the\n    default) carries the prelude tree ahead of the body; `:linked` requires\n@@ -2315,8 +2363,8 @@\n    the task's runtime state with `(js/init!)`.\"\n   ([packet] (lower-packet packet {}))\n   ([packet {:keys [prelude], :or {prelude :bundled}}]\n-   (let [main (names/canonicalize (app* 'js/run-main (lower-unit packet)))]\n-     (with-runtime prelude main))))\n+   (let [main (names/canonicalize (app* 'js/run-main (lower-unit* packet)))]\n+     (u/annotate-call-sites (with-runtime prelude main)))))\n \n \n (def program-medium\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc\nindex 95de7898..6ba172ec 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude.cljc\n@@ -1893,6 +1893,22 @@\n          (js/get-prop js.rt/global name)\n          (js/throw-reference-error\n            (js/str-concat name {:js/str \" is not defined\"}))))]\n+    [js/global-set\n+     ;; Assignment to a name no lexical binding reaches: SetMutableBinding of\n+     ;; a STRICT object environment record (ES2022 §9.1.1.3.3) over the heap\n+     ;; global object (design §3.1.4 ruling 4, §3.7). HasBinding is false, so\n+     ;; strict code refuses the implicit global with a ReferenceError naming\n+     ;; it. Otherwise the write is the global object's own [[Set]] with\n+     ;; itself as receiver: an accessor slot runs its setter and never its\n+     ;; getter, an existing writable data slot is updated with its other\n+     ;; attributes preserved, and a non-writable one (`undefined`) is a\n+     ;; TypeError. No read of the old value — assigning a reference resolves\n+     ;; the name without getting it.\n+     (fn [name v]\n+       (if (js/has-property js.rt/global name)\n+         (js/put-value js.rt/global name v)\n+         (js/throw-reference-error\n+           (js/str-concat name {:js/str \" is not defined\"}))))]\n     [js/global-typeof\n      (fn [name]\n        (if (js/has-property js.rt/global name)\n@@ -4363,8 +4379,11 @@\n \n (def module-uast\n   \"The module tree: one application whose operands are the definitions, in\n-   order, applied to a lambda that returns nil.\"\n-  (core/module-tree module-definitions []))\n+   order, applied to a lambda that returns nil. C1 finalized, like every\n+   published production tree: its `:yang/call-site` markers publish beside\n+   its manifest (see `yin.vm.linker.publish`), never inside it, so the\n+   manifest keeps schema 1 and its address does not move.\"\n+  (u/annotate-call-sites (core/module-tree module-definitions [])))\n \n \n (def module-exports\ndiff --git a/test/yang/typescript/antlr/float_address_test.cljc b/test/yang/typescript/antlr/float_address_test.cljc\nindex 51c29451..3a30cb34 100644\n--- a/test/yang/typescript/antlr/float_address_test.cljc\n+++ b/test/yang/typescript/antlr/float_address_test.cljc\n@@ -100,8 +100,8 @@\n             the JS R1+R3 exception-boundary round)\"\n     (is (= (keyword\n              (str \"segment/blake3-\"\n-                  \"6500c67e1157669d3b05f35b02bba44d\"\n-                  \"18fe305a8df49d4ba3e86254d03fbb2c\"))\n+                  \"159a54c56100fa5ee9c163eae8cdb9c3\"\n+                  \"34f9325f04985131121fb3794e66448a\"))\n            (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode prelude/uast))))))\n \n \n@@ -139,8 +139,8 @@\n             re-pinned for the JS R1+R3 exception-boundary round)\"\n     (is (= (keyword\n              (str \"segment/blake3-\"\n-                  \"82614eea8e3fb6d1042ca30e1e195f85\"\n-                  \"2f09504b133141d71e6b93d374b641c5\"))\n+                  \"df0d543a07daf58abb2512afb2312783a5\"\n+                  \"83f54f1e4f4e5a083a47103ede0848\"))\n            (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode float-program)))))\n   (testing \"decoding the program and projecting it again keeps the address\"\n     (let [bytecode (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode float-program)\ndiff --git a/test/yang/typescript/antlr/global_write_test.cljc b/test/yang/typescript/antlr/global_write_test.cljc\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 00000000..fdb63f5e\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/test/yang/typescript/antlr/global_write_test.cljc\n@@ -0,0 +1,255 @@\n+(ns yang.typescript.antlr.global-write-test\n+  \"T2 — assignment to a name no lexical binding reaches (design\n+   yang.typescript.md §3.1.4 ruling 4 and §3.7). Strict mode is always on, so\n+   the write is a strict object-environment SetMutableBinding over the heap\n+   global object (ES2022 §9.1.1.3.3), which separates three cases earlier\n+   rounds collapsed into one blanket refusal:\n+\n+   - nothing binds the name and the global object has no such property: a\n+     catchable ReferenceError NAMING it, never an implicit global;\n+   - an existing WRITABLE global property: the write SUCCEEDS — strict mode\n+     forbids creating an implicit global, not updating one already there, so\n+     `globalThis.saved = null; saved = 7;` holds at module goal too;\n+   - an existing NON-WRITABLE global property (`undefined`): a catchable\n+     TypeError, not a ReferenceError.\n+\n+   The accessor fixture pins the fourth fact: assignment resolves the\n+   reference without getting its value, so the setter runs and the getter\n+   stays silent. A retained `js/global-get` read would log `getter` first.\n+\n+   Portable (JVM/Node/Dart): every fixture is a hand-built CST packet in the\n+   `lower-portable-test` idiom, so no JVM-only parser is involved, and each\n+   program runs on all four evaluators. §3.7 script-goal DECLARATION\n+   placement — a top-level `var` becoming a property of the global object —\n+   stays the design-specified deferred slice and is not pinned here.\"\n+  (:require\n+    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n+    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as lower]\n+    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower-portable-test :as portable]\n+    [yang.typescript.antlr.prelude-parity-test :as parity]\n+    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]))\n+\n+\n+;; =============================================================================\n+;; CST forms, hand-built in the parser's own shapes\n+;; =============================================================================\n+\n+(defn- member-form\n+  \"`obj.prop` as a singleExpression form.\"\n+  [obj prop]\n+  [:singleExpression\n+   (portable/name-expr obj)\n+   [\"Dot\" \".\"]\n+   [:identifierName [:identifier [\"Identifier\" prop]]]])\n+\n+\n+(defn- str-form\n+  \"`'text'` as a singleExpression form.\"\n+  [text]\n+  [:singleExpression [:literal [\"StringLiteral\" (str \"'\" text \"'\")]]])\n+\n+\n+(defn- null-form\n+  \"`null` as a singleExpression form.\"\n+  []\n+  [:singleExpression [:literal [\"NullLiteral\" \"null\"]]])\n+\n+\n+(defn- assign-form\n+  \"`lhs = rhs` as a singleExpression form.\"\n+  [lhs rhs]\n+  [:singleExpression lhs [\"Assign\" \"=\"] rhs])\n+\n+\n+(defn- strict-eq-form\n+  \"`a === b` as a singleExpression form.\"\n+  [a b]\n+  [:singleExpression a [\"IdentityEquals\" \"===\"] b])\n+\n+\n+(defn- call-form\n+  \"`callee(arg ...)` as a singleExpression form.\"\n+  [callee & args]\n+  [:singleExpression\n+   callee\n+   [:arguments\n+    [\"OpenParen\" \"(\"]\n+    (into [:argumentList] (map (fn [a] [:argument a]) args))\n+    [\"CloseParen\" \")\"]]])\n+\n+\n+(defn- object-form\n+  \"`{a: x, b: y}` as a singleExpression form, over `[name value-form]` pairs.\"\n+  [& pairs]\n+  [:singleExpression\n+   (vec (concat [:objectLiteral [\"OpenBrace\" \"{\"]]\n+                (map (fn [[nm v]]\n+                       [:propertyAssignment\n+                        [:propertyName\n+                         [:identifierName [:identifier [\"Identifier\" nm]]]]\n+                        [\"Colon\" \":\"]\n+                        v])\n+                     pairs)\n+                [[\"CloseBrace\" \"}\"]]))])\n+\n+\n+(defn- expr-stmt\n+  \"One expression statement over a singleExpression form.\"\n+  [expr]\n+  [:expressionStatement [:expressionSequence expr] [\"SemiColon\" \";\"]])\n+\n+\n+(defn- return-stmt\n+  \"`return expr;` over a singleExpression form.\"\n+  [expr]\n+  [:returnStatement\n+   [\"Return\" \"return\"]\n+   [:expressionSequence expr]\n+   [:eos [\"SemiColon\" \";\"]]])\n+\n+\n+(defn- block-form\n+  \"`{ stmt ... }` as a block form, over statement forms.\"\n+  [& stmts]\n+  (vec (concat [:block [\"OpenBrace\" \"{\"]]\n+               [(into [:statementList] (map (fn [s] [:statement s]) stmts))]\n+               [[\"CloseBrace\" \"}\"]])))\n+\n+\n+(defn- log-stmt\n+  \"`console.log(arg ...)` over singleExpression forms.\"\n+  [& args]\n+  (expr-stmt (apply call-form (member-form \"console\" \"log\") args)))\n+\n+\n+(defn- arrow-form\n+  \"`() => { body }` as a singleExpression form, over statement forms.\"\n+  [& body]\n+  [:singleExpression\n+   [:anonymousFunction\n+    [:arrowFunctionDeclaration\n+     [:arrowFunctionParameters [\"OpenParen\" \"(\"] [\"CloseParen\" \")\"]]\n+     [\"ARROW\" \"=>\"]\n+     [:arrowFunctionBody\n+      [\"OpenBrace\" \"{\"]\n+      [:functionBody\n+       (into [:sourceElements]\n+             (map (fn [s] [:sourceElement [:statement s]]) body))]\n+      [\"CloseBrace\" \"}\"]]]]])\n+\n+\n+(defn- try-catch-stmt\n+  \"`try { body } catch (ident) { handler }` over statement forms.\"\n+  [body ident handler]\n+  [:tryStatement\n+   [\"Try\" \"try\"]\n+   (apply block-form body)\n+   [:catchProduction\n+    [\"Catch\" \"catch\"]\n+    [\"OpenParen\" \"(\"]\n+    [:identifier [\"Identifier\" ident]]\n+    [\"CloseParen\" \")\"]\n+    (apply block-form handler)]])\n+\n+\n+;; =============================================================================\n+;; The four programs\n+;; =============================================================================\n+\n+(def ^:private absent-name\n+  \"`try { undeclaredProbe = 7; } catch (e) { console.log(e.name);\n+    console.log(e.message); }` — the guest catches the failure itself, so the\n+   pin reads both the class and the promised naming message off the error.\"\n+  (portable/program\n+    (try-catch-stmt\n+      [(expr-stmt (assign-form (portable/name-expr \"undeclaredProbe\")\n+                               (portable/num-expr \"7\")))]\n+      \"e\"\n+      [(log-stmt (member-form \"e\" \"name\"))\n+       (log-stmt (member-form \"e\" \"message\"))])))\n+\n+\n+(def ^:private writable-global\n+  \"`globalThis.saved = null; saved = 7; console.log(globalThis.saved === 7);`\n+   — the member write creates a writable global property, and the bare write\n+   to the same name updates it instead of refusing.\"\n+  (portable/program\n+    (expr-stmt (assign-form (member-form \"globalThis\" \"saved\") (null-form)))\n+    (expr-stmt (assign-form (portable/name-expr \"saved\")\n+                            (portable/num-expr \"7\")))\n+    (log-stmt (strict-eq-form (member-form \"globalThis\" \"saved\")\n+                              (portable/num-expr \"7\")))))\n+\n+\n+(def ^:private non-writable-global\n+  \"`try { undefined = 7; } catch (e) { console.log(e.name); }` — the prelude\n+   installs `undefined` as a non-writable global property, so the write is a\n+   failed [[Set]], which strict mode reports as a TypeError.\"\n+  (portable/program\n+    (try-catch-stmt\n+      [(expr-stmt (assign-form (portable/name-expr \"undefined\")\n+                               (portable/num-expr \"7\")))]\n+      \"e\"\n+      [(log-stmt (member-form \"e\" \"name\"))])))\n+\n+\n+(def ^:private accessor-global\n+  \"`Object.defineProperty(globalThis, 'acc', {get: () => { console.log('getter');\n+    return 1; }, set: () => { console.log('setter'); }}); acc = 5;` — the\n+   getter logging at all would be the retained value read the\n+   SetMutableBinding contract forbids.\"\n+  (portable/program\n+    (expr-stmt\n+      (call-form (member-form \"Object\" \"defineProperty\")\n+                 (portable/name-expr \"globalThis\")\n+                 (str-form \"acc\")\n+                 (object-form\n+                   [\"get\" (arrow-form (log-stmt (str-form \"getter\"))\n+                                      (return-stmt (portable/num-expr \"1\")))]\n+                   [\"set\" (arrow-form (log-stmt (str-form \"setter\")))])))\n+    (expr-stmt (assign-form (portable/name-expr \"acc\")\n+                            (portable/num-expr \"5\")))))\n+\n+\n+(defn- check-program\n+  \"The rendered output of one hand-built packet on all four evaluators.\"\n+  [packet expected label]\n+  (testing label\n+    (let [ast (lower/lower-packet packet)]\n+      (doseq [[backend run] parity/runners]\n+        (is (= expected (render/output (run ast)))\n+            (str label \" — \" backend))))))\n+\n+\n+(deftest absent-name-is-a-reference-error-naming-it-test\n+  (check-program\n+    absent-name\n+    {:js/out [\"ReferenceError\" \"undeclaredProbe is not defined\"],\n+     :js/uncaught nil}\n+    \"a binding-less name the global object does not hold either: a catchable\n+     ReferenceError whose message names the variable, and nothing escapes the\n+     guest's own catch\"))\n+\n+\n+(deftest existing-writable-global-assignment-succeeds-test\n+  (check-program\n+    writable-global\n+    {:js/out [\"true\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n+    \"an existing writable global property: the bare assignment writes it, so\n+     `globalThis.saved === 7` after `globalThis.saved = null; saved = 7;`\"))\n+\n+\n+(deftest non-writable-global-assignment-is-a-type-error-test\n+  (check-program\n+    non-writable-global\n+    {:js/out [\"TypeError\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n+    \"an existing NON-writable global property (`undefined`): a catchable\n+     TypeError, not the ReferenceError an absent name gets\"))\n+\n+\n+(deftest global-accessor-setter-runs-and-getter-does-not-test\n+  (check-program\n+    accessor-global\n+    {:js/out [\"setter\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n+    \"a global accessor: assignment invokes the setter once and never reads\n+     through the getter\"))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
