{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '3.1.4|3.7|global object|strict mode|port.attribution' docs/design/yang.typescript.md docs/agents/build-n-test.md && sed -n '1,140p' test/yang/typescript/antlr/prelude_parity_test.cljc && sed -n '1,140p' test/yang/typescript/antlr/lower_portable_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"docs/design/yang.typescript.md:30:with the limits of section 3.7, scripts) to the Universal AST. The TypeScript\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:85:|    | store                              | section 3.7; PHP's global scope is |\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:289:### 3.7 Script-goal globals\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:292:of the heap global object; top-level `let`, `const` and `class` live in a\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:294:global object and is not reachable by property access. The REPL's persistent\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:720:global object, the job-queue cells, the module registry `js.rt/modules` and\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:724:Python's 3,770-line prelude splits roughly into 1,000 lines of shareable\ndocs/design/yang.typescript.md:1121:global object and the global declarative environment (section 3.7).\n(ns yang.typescript.antlr.prelude-parity-test\n  \"The `js` prelude's semantics on all four VMs and every host this runs on\n   (T1 steps S1 and S2): two-form strings, ES Number::toString, ToNumber,\n   ToInt32, the operator family with exact BigInt arms, equality and order,\n   the ordered own-key map, object reads with primitive receivers, function\n   calls, the Error family, the continuation escapes, `js/init!` and the\n   console boundary.\n\n   Numbers are float64 content: a test writes one as the marker `{:n x}`,\n   which becomes `(data/float64 x)` in a program and `(cbor/float64 x)` in an\n   expectation (`:neg-zero`, `:nan`, `:inf` and `:-inf` name the specials),\n   and results compare by `cbor/content=`, which is kind strict: a bare 1 (a\n   bigint) is never a float64 1.\"\n  (:require [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [clojure.walk :as walk]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [yang.typescript.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n            [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\n            [yang.core.uast :as u]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.data :as data]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.integer :as integer]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(def ^:private opts\n  \"The composition over the real modules.\"\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\n   :capability-secret tu/secret,\n   :primitives vm/primitives,\n   :modules (-> (module/empty-registry)\n                module/register-cell-module\n                (data/register-data-module {::data/max-items 1048576})\n                (prelude/register-integer-module {::integer/max-bits 100000,\n                                                  ::integer/max-digits 4300})\n                prelude/admit)})\n\n\n(def ^:private load-semantic-ast\n  (vm/fresh-code-loader semantic/load-ast\n                        vm/ast-contract))\n\n\n(def vm-runners\n  \"Each VM's runner over the composition: ast to the finished VM.\"\n  {:ast-walker (fn [ast] (vm/eval (tu/create-vm opts) ast)),\n   :semantic (fn [ast]\n               (vm/run (load-semantic-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                          (vm/ast->datoms ast)))),\n   :stack (fn [ast]\n            (vm/run (dvm/create-vm\n                      (:image (derive/stack-image\n                                (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                      (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract)))),\n   :register (fn [ast]\n               (vm/run\n                 (rvm/create-vm\n                   (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n                   (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract))))})\n\n\n(def runners\n  (into {}\n        (map (fn [[k run]] [k (fn [ast] (vm/value (run ast)))]))\n        vm-runners))\n\n\n(defn run-with-prelude\n  \"The value of `form` (prelude notation) after `prelude-ast`, on each VM.\"\n  [prelude-ast form]\n  (let [ast (u/mark-tails (u/then prelude-ast (u/sexp->uast form)))\n        attempt (fn [run]\n                  (try (run ast)\n                       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Exception :cljs :default) e\n                         [:thrown (ex-message e)])))]\n    (into {} (map (fn [[k run]] [k (attempt run)])) runners)))\n\n\n(defn- special\n  [x]\n  (case x\n    :neg-zero (* -1.0 0.0)\n    :nan (- ##Inf ##Inf)\n    :inf ##Inf\n    :-inf ##-Inf\n    x))\n\n\n(defn- marker?\n  [x]\n  (and (map? x) (= [:n] (keys x))))\n\n\n(defn program-form\n  \"`form` with every `{:n x}` marker as float64 content, embedded as a\n   literal (on JS the carrier: a bare integral Number is an integer, and\n   one past 2^53 is refused).\"\n  [form]\n  (walk/postwalk (fn [x] (if (marker? x) (cbor/float64 (special (:n x))) x))\n                 form))\n\n\n(defn expected-value\n  \"`expected` with every `{:n x}` marker as float64 content.\"\n  [expected]\n  (program-form expected))\n\n\n(defn- same?\n  [a b]\n  (cbor/content= a b))\n\n\n(defn- throws\n  \"A form that answers the `name` of the error `expr` throws, or the value.\"\n  [expr]\n  (list 'js/try\n        (list 'fn [] expr)\n        '(fn [e] (js/get-prop e {:js/str \"name\"}))))\n\n\n(defn- av\n  \"A program form building the argument vector of `xs`.\"\n  [& xs]\n  (reduce (fn [acc a] (list 'js/vconj acc a)) [] xs))\n\n\n(defn- call-method\n  [recv method & args]\n  (list 'js/call\n        (list 'js/get-value recv {:js/str method})\n        recv\n        (reduce (fn [acc a] (list 'js/vconj acc a)) [] args)))\n(ns yang.typescript.antlr.lower-portable-test\n  \"The TypeScript lowering on every host from hand-built CST packets: no\n   parser needed, so this runs on the JVM, Node and Dart. Covers the\n   unknown-rule and typed refusals, tree validation, goldens, the\n   canonical-renaming law, site-mark survival through the projection and\n   the stage transform's routing.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n    [yang.core.names :as names]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as lower]))\n\n\n(defn packet\n  \"A CST packet from a nested form: `[rule child ...]` for a rule and\n   `[type text]` (type a string) for a token. Spans are zero-width: the\n   lowering reads them only for diagnostics. Ids are preorder, as the\n   parser numbers them, so generated names match a parsed packet's.\"\n  [form]\n  (let [out (volatile! [])]\n    (letfn [(walk\n              [f]\n              (let [id (count @out)]\n                (if (string? (first f))\n                  (vswap! out conj {:id id, :kind :token, :type (first f),\n                                    :text (second f), :span [0 0]})\n                  (do (vswap! out conj nil)\n                      (let [kids (mapv walk (rest f))]\n                        (vswap! out assoc id {:id id, :kind :rule,\n                                              :rule (name (first f)),\n                                              :children kids, :span [0 0]}))))\n                id))]\n      (walk form))\n    {:yang.cst/version 1,\n     :yang.cst/unit [:hand 0],\n     :yang.cst/grammar \"hand\",\n     :yang.cst/outcome :yang.cst/ok,\n     :yang.cst/root 0,\n     :yang.cst/nodes @out,\n     :yang.cst/complete true}))\n\n\n(defn program\n  \"A program packet over the statement forms `stmts`.\"\n  [& stmts]\n  (packet (into [:program\n                 (into [:sourceElements]\n                       (map (fn [s] [:sourceElement [:statement s]]) stmts))]\n                [[\"EOF\" \"<EOF>\"]])))\n\n\n(defn num-expr\n  [text]\n  [:singleExpression [:literal [:numericLiteral [\"DecimalLiteral\" text]]]])\n\n\n(defn name-expr\n  [text]\n  [:singleExpression [:identifierName [:identifier [\"Identifier\" text]]]])\n\n\n(defn var-stmt\n  [modifier id init]\n  [:variableStatement\n   [:varModifier [(str modifier) modifier]]\n   [:variableDeclarationList\n    [:variableDeclaration\n     [:identifierOrKeyWord [:identifier [\"Identifier\" id]]]\n     [\"Assign\" \"=\"]\n     init]]\n   [\"SemiColon\" \";\"]])\n\n\n(defn log-stmt\n  \"The expression statement `console.log(arg);` over singleExpression form\n   `arg`.\"\n  [arg]\n  [:expressionStatement\n   [:expressionSequence\n    [:singleExpression\n     [:singleExpression\n      (name-expr \"console\")\n      [\"Dot\" \".\"]\n      [:identifierName [:identifier [\"Identifier\" \"log\"]]]]\n     [:arguments\n      [\"OpenParen\" \"(\"]\n      [:argumentList [:argument arg]]\n      [\"CloseParen\" \")\"]]]]\n   [\"SemiColon\" \";\"]])\n\n\n(def ^:private var-x\n  (program (var-stmt \"var\" \"x\" (num-expr \"1\"))))\n\n\n(def ^:private while-loop\n  (program [:iterationStatement\n            [\"While\" \"while\"] [\"OpenParen\" \"(\"]\n            [:expressionSequence (name-expr \"x\")]\n            [\"CloseParen\" \")\"]\n            [:statement [:emptyStatement_ [\"SemiColon\" \";\"]]]]))\n\n\n(def ^:private function-f\n  (program [:functionDeclaration\n            [\"Function_\" \"function\"]\n            [:identifier [\"Identifier\" \"f\"]]\n            [:callSignature [\"OpenParen\" \"(\"] [\"CloseParen\" \")\"]]\n            [\"OpenBrace\" \"{\"]\n            [:functionBody]\n            [\"CloseBrace\" \"}\"]]))\n\n\n(def ^:private class-a\n  \"class A { m() { return 1; } }\"\n  [:classDeclaration\n   [\"Class\" \"class\"]\n   [:identifier [\"Identifier\" \"A\"]]\n   [:classHeritage]\n   [:classTail\n    [\"OpenBrace\" \"{\"]\n    [:classElement\n     [:propertyMemberDeclaration\n      [:propertyMemberBase]\n      [:classElementName\n       [:propertyName [:identifierName [:identifier [\"Identifier\" \"m\"]]]]]\n      [:callSignature [\"OpenParen\" \"(\"] [\"CloseParen\" \")\"]]\n      [\"OpenBrace\" \"{\"]\n      [:functionBody\n       [:sourceElements\n        [:sourceElement\n         [:statement\n          [:returnStatement\n           [\"Return\" \"return\"]\n           [:expressionSequence (num-expr \"1\")]\n           [:eos [\"SemiColon\" \";\"]]]]]]]\n      [\"CloseBrace\" \"}\"]]]\n    [\"CloseBrace\" \"}\"]]])\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
